{
  "step": 3,
  "id": "application-intake",
  "label": "S6 application_intake（合成简历 → candidate + application；F1：新建时钉住 rubric）",
  "tool": {
    "name": "recruitment_application_intake",
    "description": "S6 resume intake. Reads one local resume file (PDF or DOCX; the media type is sniffed from the CONTENT, so the extension never decides whether a file is accepted), resolves the candidate by exact normalized phone/email only (names are never used for identity), and reports THREE independent states: (1) application_action=CREATED|REUSED — the application identity is (candidate, job) while lifecycle_status=ACTIVE, never the file hash, so a new material for the same candidate+job reuses that application; (2) structure_saved=true|false — whether this call appended a new resume_version carrying a validated structured result (resume_version rows are immutable); (3) resume_version_id / resume_version_no / resume_version_action=APPENDED|UNCHANGED — the version now in effect, which application.resume_version_id points at. A byte-identical replay returns REUSED/UNCHANGED and writes nothing. If phone and email are both unreadable it refuses with BLOCKED_BY_REVIEW and writes nothing. Only a native_text phone/email from the reader may auto-merge; OCR / agent-read values stay weak (BLOCKED_BY_REVIEW), which is unaffected by the accepted-file-format list. It never merges candidates. Writes only through SET LOCAL recruitment.actor_id. Optionally accepts structured_json (the structuring agent result for the SAME material): it is validated against this material block index, rejected results write nothing (old facts untouched), and accepted results set the five business fields state while preserving converter_state. RUBRIC PIN: when the target job's current_rubric_version_id points at a version that is APPROVED at call time, a NEW application is created with application.rubric_version_id pinned to exactly that version (D-21/D-48: current is the explicit pointer, never max(version_no)). When the job has no approved current rubric the field stays EMPTY and intake still succeeds — receiving a resume must not require a rubric first; recruitment_application_stage_advance pins it later once the rubric is approved. Only the create path pins: an existing (REUSED) application is never re-pinned here.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "path": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Absolute path of a local resume file (PDF or DOCX). The media type is sniffed from the file CONTENT, never from the extension. Must exist and must be inside the configured allowed_roots (fail-closed: any other path is rejected with FORBIDDEN). Images are rejected with reason_code=IMAGE_REQUIRES_VISION (S6 has no OCR/vision attribution step); RTF and other containers are rejected with READER_FAILED(reason_code=UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA)."
        },
        "job_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Target job id, UUID text form (e.g. 11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000401)."
        },
        "structured_json": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional: the structuring agent's JSON result for the SAME material, as a JSON string (<= 400000 characters). When present it is validated against the block index of this material (the same serialize()/validate() used by recruitment_resume_serialize + recruitment_structure_validate); a rejected result writes nothing. When present the five business fields take their state from this result (converter state is preserved separately). When absent, behavior is unchanged."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "path",
        "job_id"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
